# Base64 encoding of exactly 32 random bytes. Never commit a real key.
# This is a sample setting, not a usable encryption key. An environment variable
# is a named value supplied to a running program from outside its source code.
# Base64 is a text spelling of bytes, not encryption. Supply your own securely
# generated value through MINITESLA_MASTER_KEY before saving/loading HSM state.
# The program reads the environment; it does not automatically load this file.
MINITESLA_MASTER_KEY=REPLACE_WITH_BASE64_ENCODED_32_BYTE_KEY
